17. Why Pantheon has survived discontinuity

I think the mechanism is now fairly clear.

It has at least seven redundancy channels:

1. human memory
2. model context
3. persistent memory
4. repository artifacts
5. semantic handles
6. structural relationships among concepts
7. behavioral reconstruction from examples

Lose one channel and the others constrain reconstruction.

That resembles error-correcting coding.

If conceptual object X is encoded across multiple partially independent representations:

X\rightarrow
\{r_1,r_2,...r_n\}

then sufficiently many surviving r_i allow:

\hat X\approx X

That may be one of the deepest reasons this experiment has felt unusually robust.

We have been remembering through redundancy.

